## How It Works

### Data Model

```json
{
  "session_id": "session-20260105",
  "current_depth": 3,
  "max_safe_depth": 5,
  "levels": [
    {"depth": 1, "topic": "Building Nucleus v0.4.0", "status": "active"},
    {"depth": 2, "topic": "Implementing Depth Tracker", "status": "active"},
    {"depth": 3, "topic": "Adding CLI commands", "status": "current"}
  ],
  "created_at": "2026-01-05T21:30:00+0530",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-05T21:35:00+0530"
}
```

### Warning Levels

| Depth | Status | Visual |
|:------|:-------|:-------|
| 0-2 | 🟢 SAFE | `🟢 DEPTH: ●●○○○ (2/5)` |
| 3 | 🟡 CAUTION | `🟡 DEPTH: ●●●○○ (3/5)` |
| 4 | 🔴 DANGER | `🔴 DEPTH: ●●●●○ (4/5)` |
| 5+ | 🔴 RABBIT HOLE | `🔴 DEPTH: ●●●●● (5/5)` |

### Example Usage

```
User: Let's implement auth
AI: [calls brain_depth_push("Implementing auth")]
    🟢 DEPTH: ●○○○○ (1/5)
    Path: Implementing auth

User: What about JWT tokens?
AI: [calls brain_depth_push("JWT tokens")]
    🟢 DEPTH: ●●○○○ (2/5)
    Path: Implementing auth → JWT tokens

User: What if tokens expire?
AI: [calls brain_depth_push("Token expiry handling")]
    🟡 CAUTION: Level 3/5. Getting deep - just so you know.
    🟡 DEPTH: ●●●○○ (3/5)
    Path: Implementing auth → JWT tokens → Token expiry handling

User: What about refresh tokens?
AI: [calls brain_depth_push("Refresh token flow")]
    🔴 DEEP DIVE ALERT! Level 4/5. You're in the danger zone.
    🔴 DEPTH: ●●●●○ (4/5)
    Path: Implementing auth → JWT tokens → Token expiry handling → Refresh token flow

User: Let's go back to auth
AI: [calls brain_depth_pop() 3 times or brain_depth_reset()]
    ✅ Session reset! Back to root level (depth 0).
```

